## multi_documentation_hub_and_forum_view

### Current Progress
- **Reference and architecture discovery** - ✅ Complete
- **Documentation schema and backend domain** - ✅ Complete
- **Shared documentation shell and editor boundary** - ✅ Complete
- **Multi-documentation routes and management** - ✅ Complete
- **Forum documentation adapter** - ✅ Complete
- **Discovery, verification, and specs** - ✅ Complete

The 2026-08-17 worker pass completed the independent documentation domain,
migration 036 and fresh schema/permissions, lifecycle/Trash providers,
visibility/ownership/revision policy, manifest/article/search APIs, content-free
realtime, SEO invalidation, and dynamic public sitemap discovery. Private set
and subscription policy is service-backed and fail closed.

The frontend now provides the multi-set `/doc` directory and nested guide
routes, dedicated creation/settings/guide-editor routes, shared TipTap editor
and sanitized renderer, stable heading anchors, responsive tokenized shell,
search, adjacent navigation, conflict handling, dirty-navigation Prompt, and
realtime refetch. `/forum/docs/...` uses the same shell over the forum-owned
bounded projection and routes edits through the existing forum editor without
documentation storage imports or writes.

Durable contracts are recorded in `.specs/documentation_spec` and every affected
route/backend/frontend/realtime/cache/security/migration card. `integrate/`
remains untouched and reference-only.

